All right, here's one suggestion that will change *that* - make the
walls of the maze move around randomly (1 change every ~20 turns.) New
passages will open up, new traps appear (except, of course, for
holes). Combine that with undiggable walls/floors and no-teleport and
it'll soon be driving you bonkers.

Alternatively, the maze could stay the same but it would be *totally*
unmappable in any way - even by walking around. No matter how often
you traversed a particular passage, you'd only ever be able to
remember the section of the maze within your immediate vision. (Here's
one instance where the Eyes of the Overworld could provide a huge
advantage.) (Come to think of it I like this idea better; there's
something sinister about it.)

Give the Minotaur intrinsic regeneration and an invulnerability to
edged weapons. (In some versions I've read that Theseus *beat* the
Minotaur to death, in others that he killed it with a sword, but this
would make the encounter a little less wombat-friendly at least.) Also
double its current damage values.

To make things a little easier, you could have a "ball of thread"
tool; attach one end to any dungeon feature (door, sink, stairs,
boulder, etc.) and you can walk as far as you want on that level, with
the thread providing a path back.

